Fix metrics-wrapper bug: setDefaultDispatcher() for smoke/backtest injection

src/lib/agents/shared/dispatchers/index.ts
- Add setDefaultDispatcher(d | null) — overrides the cached default
  with a specific dispatcher instance. Pass null to revert to env-based
  selection.
- Sets cachedMode to '__override__' so subsequent env-based queries
  rebuild the dispatcher only when explicitly reset.

scripts/run-smoke-test.ts
- Wrap FileQueueDispatcher.dispatch with timing + token capture
- Call setDefaultDispatcher(wrapped) BEFORE calling scoreChart() so the
  orchestrator's getDefaultDispatcher() returns THIS wrapped instance
  (not a fresh one from env vars).
- Capture per-dispatch usage tokens (input/output/cached) from
  DispatchResponse.usage
- Print summary: total dispatches, wall clock, avg per-dispatch,
  total tokens (in/out/cached)

Bug context (from smoke test 1 on exemplar 09):
The previous run reported "Total dispatches: 0" because the local
wrapped FileQueueDispatcher was never injected as the cached default.
scoreChart() ran getDefaultDispatcher() which created its own (un-wrapped)
FileQueueDispatcher per env vars, so timing capture never fired even
though the actual dispatches succeeded. Real count was 5 dispatches.

After this fix: timing wrapper actually captures each dispatch.

368 vitest passing. TypeScript type-check clean.
